WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:05.980
<i>Everyone is searching for a new world</i>

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:12.090
<i>to attain that overflowing dream.</i>

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:17.660
<i>They all jump over the horizon,</i>

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:26.430
<i>regardless of what lies beyond.</i>

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:34.180
<i>We've run,</i>

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:36.650
<i>we've dived into hope,</i>

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:39.520
<i>and forgotten only courage.</i>

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:44.260
<i>And we've been swept away by the crowd</i>

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:48.920
<i>only to lose something dear to us.</i>

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:54.600
<i>I smile with a twisted face,</i>

00:00:54.600 --> 00:01:01.270
<i>and it was the best smile I could put on.</i>

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:04.640
<i>The inside of my mask overflowed with tears</i>

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:12.280
<i>so I covered my wet mask
with yet another mask.</i>

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:17.190
<i>I continue to walk through
the flat battleground,</i>

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:22.430
<i>and I struggle, unable to warp.</i>

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:32.540
<i>The dream waits quietly on a cape far away.</i>

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:37.280
<i>Even if I fumble around clumsily,</i>

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:42.010
<i>I'm sure I'll still be
able to make it there.</i>

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:53.380
That's not an earthquake...

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:56.390
<i>Rio-san! I bet it's
Narumi-san and the others!</i>

00:01:56.390 --> 00:01:57.820
Let's give it our all!

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:22.770
Guess there's no turning back now!

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:30.680
It might be better to jump down
than continue ahead.

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:41.730
-Mines.
-Oh, man.

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:43.860
We're being completely toyed with...

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:52.880
Narumi's younger brother...

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:55.150
I don't know if it's goodwill or pity,

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:59.480
but conspiring with those
demons makes him no different.

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:03.150
If he too must die, then so be it.

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:08.760
"Scanner of Darkness"

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:19.130
Damn! They've got traps
everywhere you go!

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:21.800
Has everything so far
gone as they expected?

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:22.800
No luck.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:26.740
Every other path has been
demolished and made impassible.

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:29.510
It looks like the power to
the elevators has been cut too.

00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:33.010
It's just like the Hunter who
went after Eyes the other day.

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:36.580
These Hunters are trying
to match wits with us!

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:39.090
Maybe someone's testing you now

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:42.520
just like how you tested me before?

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:46.460
So this entire building
is filled with traps?

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:48.630
Looks like the only things with power

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:52.930
are the lights, the internal phones,
and the security system...

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:54.700
Security system?

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:56.200
Surveillance cameras.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:59.470
The lights came on when
we entered the lobby.

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:01.980
The Hunters are watching us.

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:04.380
Which means there's at least one enemy

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:06.550
in the security room.

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:09.120
It'll be really hard to make
any moves with them watching us.

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:11.120
Should we take care of them first?

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:14.890
No. I doubt they'll
go down without a fight.

00:04:14.890 --> 00:04:16.260
It would be a waste of time.

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:18.930
But they know exactly where we are...

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:23.460
it's game over once they
detonate a trap we get close to.

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:24.900
No.

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:27.330
Not if it's done
with wires like earlier.

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:30.900
"Out of Service Area"?

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:34.770
The transceivers you brought
are probably unusable too.

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:38.750
You're right.
Is it electronic jamming?

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:41.580
Yeah, they've got their bases covered.

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:44.920
But now they probably can't use
wireless communication either.

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:48.390
For now, let's make sure
we avoid the telephones.

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:51.290
That's fine, but now what do we do?

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:54.760
So much as graze a wire and the
anti-personnel mines explode.

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:57.030
We'll be mincemeat.

00:04:57.030 --> 00:05:00.070
The lattices are 6 inches on each side

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:02.400
and about 8 inches high...

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:05.870
It would be too hard
to walk even on tiptoe...

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:14.400
Our only option is to
get across somehow, but...

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:21.650
What's he doing?

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:24.120
Could you give me a hand here?

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:25.560
Yeah, sure.

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:27.390
Eh? Hold on, Ryoko!

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:30.660
Why should we have to help him?!

00:05:34.570 --> 00:05:37.570
Then do you have any good ideas?

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:39.110
If so, then let's hear 'em.

00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:41.700
If not, then be quiet and help us.

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:46.340
Do you expect me to listen to
you with no explanation at all?

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:50.380
Are you any good at
this sort of thing?

00:05:55.090 --> 00:05:56.390
What are they...?!

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:07.730
I can't believe you're
making me do this!

00:06:07.730 --> 00:06:10.600
It's all yours since
you're the most energetic!

00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:15.110
I can't do anything this dangerous;

00:06:15.110 --> 00:06:16.880
I suck at physical stuff!

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:18.980
Who says?

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:20.810
Bastard!

00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:27.110
Damn it!

00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:30.720
Made it.

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:44.560
Alright!

00:07:00.490 --> 00:07:04.010
<i>He is childish,
but he's also resourceful.</i>

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:08.390
Kiyotaka Narumi's
younger brother, huh?

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:17.500
Now then, we'll have to
hoof it up the emergency stairs

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:19.740
on either the left or the right...

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:20.730
Which do we take?

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:26.880
What's the easiest place
in a room to booby-trap?

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:28.280
A door.

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:31.450
Then why would you choose
a door that's closed?

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:35.320
There's a good chance both
staircases have traps on them.

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:39.290
If so, then the trap you can
anticipate is the easiest to deal with.

00:07:39.290 --> 00:07:40.690
Correct.

00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:44.560
It's ten years too early
for them to be testing us!

00:08:00.850 --> 00:08:01.780
<i>Rio-san!</i>

00:08:01.780 --> 00:08:05.180
<i>Narumi-san and the others
will be here soon to rescue us!</i>

00:08:05.180 --> 00:08:11.060
We can't just sit here
while they fight, can we?

00:08:11.060 --> 00:08:12.990
<i>No, we sure can't, Rio-san!</i>

00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:14.760
We have to hurry!

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:21.730
The intruders have entered the
northern emergency stairway.

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:23.290
Give them some light.

00:08:28.810 --> 00:08:31.440
The bastards are leading us!

00:08:37.880 --> 00:08:40.120
How many stories was
this building, again?

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:42.790
We have to climb all the way up?
This sucks...

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:44.560
Stop complaining!

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:46.960
I'm in good enough
physical condition for this,

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:49.360
<i>but I am worried about you two...</i>

00:08:51.660 --> 00:08:54.570
It would seem there's
no need to worry just yet...

00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:58.500
What the?

00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:01.910
Looks like they want us
to enter the 5th floor.

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:05.280
How kind of them to leave
the door open for us.

00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:08.650
Are you sure we shouldn't
figure out a way up the stairs?

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:11.950
How do we do that when the
staircase has collapsed?

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:15.860
So you want to walk straight
into a trap then?

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:20.430
We've been in a trap since the
moment we entered this building.

00:09:20.430 --> 00:09:22.860
There's no harm in
accepting one more invitation.

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:25.630
Hey! You're the one who
said not to rush ahead!

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:30.290
Whatever. You're all the same.

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:40.750
I'm home. Ayumu?

00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:44.180
Oh? Why's it pitch dark?

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:50.490
Could you get me some water, please?

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:56.660
Fine! I'll get it myself!

00:10:03.270 --> 00:10:07.640
"Madoka...I've gone to a friend's place.

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:10.130
There's some stew in the pot."

00:10:11.780 --> 00:10:18.550
<i>He lied to me again!</i>

00:10:24.860 --> 00:10:28.260
Come on, I'm getting sick of this!

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:32.470
It looks like we can't explode it
like we did with the door trap.

00:10:32.470 --> 00:10:34.400
Nope.

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:36.540
See all those containers?

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:39.810
I don't know how many
explosives they have in them,

00:10:39.810 --> 00:10:44.070
but the entire floor would
probably collapse if they went off.

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:47.210
But we can't go up without clearing this

00:10:47.210 --> 00:10:51.820
and getting to the emergency
stairs on the other side.

00:10:51.820 --> 00:10:53.420
Right?

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:55.750
These guys sure have a
lot of time on their hands.

00:10:57.220 --> 00:11:00.190
It's about 5 feet 7 inches high...

00:11:00.190 --> 00:11:03.000
It's not too high for me to jump over...

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:06.070
Forget about it.
We still have a long ways to go.

00:11:06.070 --> 00:11:08.630
What good would wasting
your strength now be?

00:11:08.630 --> 00:11:12.040
It would be all over
before that, anyway.

00:11:13.210 --> 00:11:16.040
The empty area at the
top is too suspicious.

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:17.910
Take a close look at the ceiling.

00:11:29.090 --> 00:11:30.420
Lasers?

00:11:30.420 --> 00:11:31.420
Yeah.

00:11:31.420 --> 00:11:33.760
Try to go over the wires
and you'll trip the lasers,

00:11:33.760 --> 00:11:37.300
which will set off an explosion.

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:39.300
Pretty sneaky.

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:42.930
Does that mean our only option
is to dismantle the bombs?

00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:53.210
We have neither the time nor the tools.

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:54.910
Then what do we do?

00:11:54.910 --> 00:11:58.280
If we can't go over, then we go under.

00:11:58.280 --> 00:12:00.220
It's simple.

00:12:00.220 --> 00:12:01.580
Under?

00:12:12.900 --> 00:12:15.530
Do you notice anything about this room?

00:12:15.530 --> 00:12:17.840
It's a conference room.

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:19.870
It would've been a pretty sweet one

00:12:19.870 --> 00:12:21.440
had it been finished.

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:24.010
This hotel was abandoned
before completion

00:12:24.010 --> 00:12:26.810
when the bubble economy collapsed.

00:12:26.810 --> 00:12:29.150
So what's your point?

00:12:29.150 --> 00:12:33.640
That it was planned out to be a
flawless and intelligent building.

00:12:36.190 --> 00:12:37.590
What's this?

00:12:56.110 --> 00:13:00.450
How did you know there was a
wiring space beneath the floor?

00:13:00.450 --> 00:13:04.120
Buildings like this are
all the same on the inside.

00:13:04.120 --> 00:13:06.890
-Hey, let's get a move-on!
-Yeah, yeah...

00:13:06.890 --> 00:13:07.880
No.

00:13:10.190 --> 00:13:13.360
There's probably no need
to play with them anymore.

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:14.990
What do you mean?

00:13:14.990 --> 00:13:17.360
Up ahead is probably no different.

00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:21.030
There are probably traps like
this on every other floor

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:23.240
and set up so we have
to pass through them

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:24.840
to climb higher.

00:13:24.840 --> 00:13:27.240
I don't know how many
traps there are left,

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:29.310
but there's no reason
to be good-natured enough

00:13:29.310 --> 00:13:31.140
to play with each and every one.

00:13:31.140 --> 00:13:33.150
So you want to defeat their plan?

00:13:33.150 --> 00:13:36.150
Even if we did clear every trap,

00:13:36.150 --> 00:13:39.180
there's no guarantee we could
rescue the hostages safely.

00:13:39.180 --> 00:13:40.250
Right?

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:42.050
Yeah, you have a point...

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:44.660
You got any specific ideas in mind?

00:13:44.660 --> 00:13:47.730
Let me borrow a knife
if you brought one.

00:13:47.730 --> 00:13:48.950
A knife?

00:13:51.400 --> 00:13:53.920
What're you up to?

00:13:59.470 --> 00:14:00.630
Here we are.

00:14:10.220 --> 00:14:13.390
Go to the electrical room and reset
the circuit breakers at once.

00:14:13.390 --> 00:14:14.690
Yes, sir!

00:14:14.690 --> 00:14:18.890
Planning to continue ahead while
you're not being watched, are you?

00:14:18.890 --> 00:14:21.530
For the brother of Kiyotaka Narumi,

00:14:21.530 --> 00:14:23.760
your thinking is too weak...

00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:27.230
<i>It looks like Narumi-san and
the others are fighting back!</i>

00:14:27.230 --> 00:14:28.130
Now's our chance.

00:14:28.130 --> 00:14:31.330
Let's hurry while the
surveillance monitors are offline!

00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:41.280
I didn't know you were hiding that!
Wow!

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:51.690
There we go...

00:14:53.430 --> 00:14:56.000
There's no feed from the 5th floor!

00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:59.900
And there's no sign of the
intruders on any other floors!

00:14:59.900 --> 00:15:05.200
Which means that they're
still on the 5th floor...

00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:06.930
What are they up to?

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:11.210
Turn the elevators on.

00:15:11.210 --> 00:15:13.880
Go check out what's
happening on the 5th floor.

00:15:13.880 --> 00:15:16.780
But the 5th floor should
be pitch black now.

00:15:16.780 --> 00:15:21.520
What if they're planning
to ambush us in the dark?

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:26.060
Simply eliminate them if they
have any such foolish intentions.

00:15:26.060 --> 00:15:28.890
<i>You are combat professionals.</i>

00:15:28.890 --> 00:15:30.260
Understood.

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:39.230
We're going to the 5th floor!

00:16:15.670 --> 00:16:17.310
We're unable to locate the targets.

00:16:17.310 --> 00:16:18.210
What?

00:16:18.210 --> 00:16:19.780
They don't appear to be on this floor.

00:16:19.780 --> 00:16:21.210
Impossible!

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:24.180
Then where did they go?!

00:16:26.890 --> 00:16:29.620
Go to the top floor!
The hostages have escaped!

00:16:29.620 --> 00:16:32.890
This time handcuff them
so they don't get away!

00:16:32.890 --> 00:16:35.030
Once you're done with that,
scour each floor

00:16:35.030 --> 00:16:38.000
one by one until you've
found the intruders!

00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:39.120
Got that?!

00:17:03.890 --> 00:17:04.910
What was that?!

00:17:07.030 --> 00:17:09.860
-Well?
-No good, it won't move.

00:17:31.950 --> 00:17:33.690
What was that?

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:36.090
Ow...

00:17:36.090 --> 00:17:37.890
-You okay?
-Yes...

00:17:38.760 --> 00:17:40.690
-There they are!
-We've been spotted!

00:17:41.730 --> 00:17:42.960
Stop!

00:17:45.230 --> 00:17:46.530
Damn it!

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:51.740
Damn you, Ayumu Narumi!

00:17:51.740 --> 00:17:53.500
How on earth?!

00:17:56.240 --> 00:17:59.180
How did you get to the top floor?

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:02.440
The Hunters gave us an elevator ride.

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:04.680
The Hunters?

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:07.420
We turned the lights off
and waited above the elevator

00:18:07.420 --> 00:18:10.050
for them to come fix the problem.

00:18:22.670 --> 00:18:25.940
And then right before the
elevator arrived at the top floor,

00:18:25.940 --> 00:18:29.600
we stopped it by triggering
the anti-shock safety system

00:18:37.780 --> 00:18:40.810
and then brought you out
during that brief moment.

00:18:51.830 --> 00:18:55.170
But how did you know
the elevator would move?

00:18:55.170 --> 00:18:58.570
They had set complicated
traps on all those floors.

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:03.700
There was no doubt that
they had used the elevators.

00:19:04.640 --> 00:19:07.050
<i>That's our Narumi-san!</i>

00:19:07.050 --> 00:19:09.010
You two did good too.

00:19:09.010 --> 00:19:11.850
You broke yourselves free so quickly.

00:19:11.850 --> 00:19:14.850
<i>That was thanks to Rio-san, of course!</i>

00:19:14.850 --> 00:19:17.720
I'm always prepared for the unexpected.

00:19:17.720 --> 00:19:20.090
You probably didn't
even need our help...

00:19:20.090 --> 00:19:24.200
Who was it who wanted to take on
a couple automatic rifles again?!

00:19:24.200 --> 00:19:26.870
Cut me some slack, will ya?

00:19:26.870 --> 00:19:29.030
You're as stupid as ever.

00:19:29.870 --> 00:19:30.840
This is bad!

00:19:32.540 --> 00:19:34.340
Everyone, run!

00:19:34.340 --> 00:19:35.810
What's going on?!

00:19:35.810 --> 00:19:37.840
The electronic jamming has stopped!

00:19:37.840 --> 00:19:40.140
Any number of bombs can
be remotely detonated now!

00:21:05.930 --> 00:21:11.630
<i>A sweet scent washes into my throat</i>

00:21:11.630 --> 00:21:18.330
<i>and my feelings continuously overflow...</i>

00:21:30.450 --> 00:21:36.490
<i>Don't look at me with that same gaze</i>

00:21:36.490 --> 00:21:42.130
<i>that's like you're following a soccer ball.</i>

00:21:42.130 --> 00:21:48.040
<i>I've already grown used to
my third year at the office,</i>

00:21:48.040 --> 00:21:54.610
<i>but did I lose something instead?</i>

00:21:54.610 --> 00:22:00.350
<i>Those days long ago when we
would talk about anything...</i>

00:22:00.350 --> 00:22:05.550
<i>We're finally old enough now</i>

00:22:05.550 --> 00:22:11.390
<i>to have those slightly awkward
discussions about love.</i>

00:22:11.390 --> 00:22:23.000
<i>A single day seems so long,
but a whole year ends so quickly.</i>

00:22:23.000 --> 00:22:28.780
<i>A whole year seems so short,</i>

00:22:28.780 --> 00:22:35.080
<i>but how well will I be able
to live the rest of my life?</i>

00:22:39.250 --> 00:22:41.190
Time for Hiyono's Useful News Report!

00:22:41.190 --> 00:22:45.120
Irises fall, flower petals fall...

00:22:45.120 --> 00:22:46.730
The heavens will know, the earth
will know, and someone will know.

00:22:46.730 --> 00:22:48.790
A hermit lives a thousand years,
a mayfly only a moment.

00:22:48.790 --> 00:22:50.200
Are materialistic people

00:22:50.200 --> 00:22:52.460
crows of a black night,
herons of a moonlit night,

00:22:52.460 --> 00:22:55.170
or caged birds that long
for the clouds?

00:22:55.170 --> 00:22:57.600
Next episode's highlight
is a comedy act

00:22:57.600 --> 00:22:58.700
<i>between Narumi-san and Hiyono-chin</i>

00:22:58.700 --> 00:23:00.970
in which they pretend to be married!

00:23:00.970 --> 00:23:03.210
On the next Spiral:
Bond of Reasoning...

00:23:03.210 --> 00:23:04.540
The Lamenting Angel

00:23:04.540 --> 00:23:06.570
That's all for today's
Hiyono's Playhouse!
